📘 SQL Learning Repository
🐬 Project Overview

The SQL Learning Repository is a complete collection of MySQL & PL/SQL practice scripts, datasets, and notes created during my SQL learning journey.
It includes hands-on exercises such as table creation, constraints, joins, functions, indexing, subqueries, and PL/SQL programming.

This repository is highly useful for:

Students learning SQL

Data analysts practicing MySQL

Interview preparation

Beginners → Advanced learners who want step-by-step SQL scripts

🎯 Objective

This project was created to:

Practice SQL fundamentals and advanced concepts through structured .sql files

Understand database operations such as joins, indexing, and constraints

Learn PL/SQL logic including variables, loops, conditions, and stored procedures

Use real datasets (company.xlsx, BigData.xlsx, joins.xlsx) for practical queries

Keep all SQL learning materials in one organized repository

📂 Project Structure
SQL-Learning/
├── 1_MySQL_CreateTable_BasicQueries.sql
├── 2_SQL_Constraints_AlterTable.sql
├── 3_AutoIncrement_Joins_Part1.sql
├── 4_AutoIncrement_Joins_Part2.sql
├── 5_Index_View_Subquery_Joins.sql
├── 6_SQL_Functions_Numerical_String_Date_Coalesce_Case.sql
├── 7_PLSQL_Variables_Loops_Procedures_Functions.sql
│
├── BigData.xlsx
├── company.xlsx
├── joins.xlsx
│
└── MYSQL WORKBENCH INSTALLATION.doc

🛠️ Approach
1️⃣ SQL Basics

Creating databases & tables

INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE operations

Fundamental SELECT queries

2️⃣ Constraints & ALTER TABLE

Primary & Foreign keys

Unique, Not Null, Default

Column modification using ALTER TABLE

3️⃣ Joins & Auto-Increment

Usage of AUTO_INCREMENT

INNER, LEFT, RIGHT, FULL joins

Real-world join practice using joins.xlsx

4️⃣ Advanced SQL Features

Creating and managing VIEWS

INDEX creation and performance improvement

Single-row & multi-row subqueries

Nested queries

5️⃣ SQL Functions

Numeric functions

String functions

Date & time operations

COALESCE()

CASE expressions

6️⃣ PL/SQL Concepts

Variables & constants

IF/ELSE conditional logic

Loops: FOR, WHILE, LOOP

Arrays (VARRAY)

Procedures & Functions (IN, OUT, IN OUT)

🧪 Datasets Included
📊 1. BigData.xlsx

Used for large-table queries, grouping, filtering, and analytical functions.

🧑‍💼 2. company.xlsx

Employee / department dataset for joins, constraints, and functions practice.

🔗 3. joins.xlsx

Lightweight dataset designed only for practicing SQL JOIN queries.

