🚀 Getting Started
1️⃣ Install MySQL Server + Workbench

Open:

MYSQL WORKBENCH INSTALLATION.doc


Follow the steps to complete the installation.

2️⃣ Execute SQL Files

Run the .sql files in this order inside MySQL Workbench:

Basic Queries

Constraints

Joins

Views & Indexes

Subqueries

SQL Functions

PL/SQL Logic

3️⃣ Import Excel Data

You can import datasets using:

Table Import Wizard
or

LOAD DATA INFILE command

These datasets help run and test complex SQL queries.

🧩 Sample Topics Covered

Table creation & data insertion

Filtering, sorting & grouping

Joining multiple tables

Aggregations (SUM, AVG, COUNT)

Subqueries & nested queries

PL/SQL loops & conditional statements

Stored procedures & functions

🧠 Troubleshooting
❗ Query Error

Ensure the table exists and names are correct.

❗ Foreign Key Error

Create the parent table first.

❗ Excel Import Issues

Convert .xlsx → .csv if your MySQL version doesn’t support Excel import.

❗ Difficulty in Joins

Refer to:

3_AutoIncrement_Joins_Part1.sql

4_AutoIncrement_Joins_Part2.sql

📈 Learning Outcomes

By practicing this repository, you will learn:

How relational databases work

How to write clean, optimized SQL queries

End-to-end understanding of SQL from basics to PL/SQL

How to analyze real-world datasets using SQL

Fundamentals of database design

